- op: discuss  # 5c71
  at: '2026-08-24T09:57:17Z'  # 5c71
  by: agent  # 5c71
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5c71
  clock: 5  # 5c71
  nonce: 5c71  # 5c71
  message: "SATISFIED, on this item's own filed fixture, measured on the merged tree with\nthe held INV-pusin branch rebased on top of all four PRs — which is the exact\nconfiguration this item was filed to make safe.\n\n  ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/rust_fidelity_probe_08232026/repo\n  (exfiltrate() calls sock.send(payload); drain() calls w.write_all(x))\n\n  BEFORE the four PRs, with INV-pusin's fix applied:\n    NET-SEND  BARE confirmed        <- FALSE. This is why the branch was held.\n    FS-WRITE  BARE confirmed        <- FALSE.\n  NOW, same branch, same crate:\n    NET-SEND  confirmed_with_caveats\n              caveats: untyped_receiver, unknown_receiver_scope,\n                       analyzer_suppressed_methods, higher_fidelity_available\n              analysis_fidelity: {\"rust\": [\"rust\"]}\n    FS-WRITE  confirmed_with_caveats, same four\n    CONTROL-FSREAD  violated        <- fires in the same run, so not blindness\n\nBOTH MECHANISMS THIS ITEM NAMED ARE DISCHARGED:\n  (1) the denylist no longer SILENTLY removes a catalogued sink method — the\n      set moved to analyzer_disclosure, rust.py imports it, and the nine names\n      it hides from rust.yaml are disclosed (PR #500). The denylist itself is\n      untouched, because WI-bakak's 22-of-29 false callers are a real defect\n      and removing the policy would reinstate them.\n  (2) every unresolved external method call now carries the call_construct\n      stamp the disclosure reads (PR #498).\n\nTHE SEQUENCING CALL WAS RIGHT AND IS WORTH KEEPING. Merging INV-pusin's fix\nwhen it was written would have converted a right-for-the-wrong-reason\n`inconclusive` into a false `confirmed` about a function named `exfiltrate`.\nHolding it and building the disclosure first turns the same fix into a\nDISCLOSED confirm. The branch\njgstern-agent/fix/scoped-attr-ref-import-and-type-positions is rebased, green,\nand now safe to merge.\n\nNOT MEASURED: whether any real Rust repository's verdict moves from\ninconclusive to confirmed_with_caveats once that branch lands (only the\nauthored fixture was run); the false-positive direction on cpp, which the same\nbranch touches."  # 5c71
